neatvnc for FlickOS
===================

Upstream: https://github.com/any1/neatvnc (ISC). This folder is Debian
trixie's source package neatvnc 0.9.1+dfsg-1 (`apt-get source neatvnc`): the
orig tarball with its debian/ folder, which has no patches. FlickOS builds it
natively, like sfwbar.

Why (docs/design/flickos-classroom-view.md, ADR-013): Debian's libneatvnc0
is built with H.264, so it depends on libavcodec, libavfilter and libavutil,
and Debian's wayvnc then adds 53 MB to a FlickOS install (libflite1 alone is
27.6 MB). flickos-classroom-view starts wayvnc on a student's computer to
show its screen to the teacher, which never uses H.264. Built without it,
wayvnc adds 1.2 MB. Debian's own wayvnc runs on this library unchanged.

Changes to Debian's packaging:
  - debian/rules: meson -Dh264=disabled; no -dbgsym package (as sfwbar);
    GIT_DIR pointed nowhere, or meson.build would put the FlickOS repo's
    commit and branch into the version string; installs into debian/tmp,
    and debian/not-installed lists the -dev files left there.
  - debian/control: libavcodec-dev, libavfilter-dev and libavutil-dev left
    out of Build-Depends; only libneatvnc0 is built (no libneatvnc-dev).
  - debian/source/format: 3.0 (native); debian/watch removed.
  - Version 0.9.1+dfsg+flickos1 and on: above Debian's 0.9.1+dfsg-1, so apt
    takes this one; flickos-classroom-view depends on it by version.

No change to upstream's code.

To move to a new upstream or Debian release: `apt-get source neatvnc` in an
empty folder, replace everything here but debian/changelog and this file,
and make the changes above again.
